course: dictionary
lesson: 8097
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word removal can mean taking something away, or it can mean moving your furniture and belongings into a new home. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «Snow removal» is clearing snow away, so removal means getting rid of something. «The removal van arrived at nine o'clock» is about a van carrying furniture to a new house. The clue is the van: a van carries things, so removal means moving house here.
explain: The sentence about Native Americans is about real history and real people. «Forced removals» means people were made to leave their homes against their will. Here removal means taking people away from their lands, and it is a sad part of history that we remember so we do not forget it.
fact: Removal means taking something away from a place, or getting rid of it.
fact: In the UK, a removal means moving furniture and belongings from one home to another.
fact: «Removal van» and «removals company» are used in the UK, Ireland and Australia; in the US people say «moving van».
fact: «Stain removal» means getting rid of a mark, and «removal of a splinter» means taking a splinter out.
fact: In «disease, wars and forced removals took their lands and many lives», removal means people being forced from their homes, which was a serious and painful part of history.
exercise: «The removal van arrived at nine o'clock to take the sofa.» What does removal mean in this sentence? | *Moving furniture and belongings to a new home | Clearing snow from the road | Taking a splinter out | Getting rid of a stain
exercise: What does «snow removal» mean? | *Clearing snow away | Building a snowman | Sledging down a hill | Making the snow bigger
exercise: What does removal mean in «the removal of a splinter»? | Eating a splinter | Painting a splinter | Putting a splinter in | *Taking the splinter out
test: Mum says the removals company is coming on Saturday. What is happening? | The family is going swimming | *Furniture and belongings are being moved to a new home | Someone is cleaning the windows | The garden is being watered
test: «The removal of the old tooth was quick.» What does removal mean? | *Taking the tooth out | Brushing the tooth | Counting the teeth | Growing a new tooth
exam: Which sentence uses removal to mean moving furniture to a new home? | *«The removal van was full of boxes and beds.» | «Stain removal is easy with this spray.» | «The removal of the splinter did not hurt.» | «Snow removal cleared the car park before school.»
